From 36391cac67477a7ccbd96f25bb17fcc1aba8d2a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:11:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/48] soc: qcom: apr: install the GPR callback before probing
 the service

apr_device_probe() assigned adev->svc.callback only after the driver's
probe returned. A driver may issue a synchronous request from its own
probe - q6apm asks the DSP for the SPF state - and the reply can arrive
while probe is still running. gpr_do_rx_callback() drops packets for a
service with no callback, so setting it afterwards loses that reply and
the request always times out.

Set the callback before probing.

Imported from BigfootACA/linux full-v7.1.3 (fdb8767545), the Xiaomi Pad 8
Pro (xiaomi-piano, SM8750) mainline tree. Original author: Junhao Xie
<bigfoot@radxa.com>.
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c
index ea7f83916..8fe72daa2 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c
@@ -367,9 +367,19 @@ static int apr_device_probe(struct device *dev)
 	struct apr_driver *adrv = to_apr_driver(dev->driver);
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Install the response callback before probing. A driver may issue a
+	 * synchronous request from its own probe - q6apm asks the DSP for the
+	 * SPF state - and the reply can arrive while probe is still running.
+	 * gpr_do_rx_callback() drops packets for a service with no callback,
+	 * so setting it afterwards loses that reply and the request always
+	 * times out, no matter how long it waits.
+	 */
+	adev->svc.callback = adrv->gpr_callback;
+
 	ret = adrv->probe(adev);
-	if (!ret)
-		adev->svc.callback = adrv->gpr_callback;
+	if (ret)
+		adev->svc.callback = NULL;
 
 	return ret;
 }
